# local: one example environment. One file per environment; the deploy
# script takes the environment's NAME and derives every other target fact
# from here, so a script cannot assume one cluster while acting on another.
# Every environment uses the same service names: each cluster's CoreDNS
# resolves .test to its own edge, so flipr.test is this cluster's flipr from
# inside it, and EDGE_PORT is how the host reaches it. Nothing here is a
# secret. Copy this file to add an environment.
ENV=local
CLUSTER=local
CTX=k3d-local
EDGE_PORT=9800
DATA_ROOT="$HOME/var/local"
